# Git for Windows checks text files out with CRLF by default
# (`core.autocrlf=true`, which is what GitHub's windows-latest runner has),
# and that broke `xtask::man`'s byte-exact gate: `clap_mangen` writes LF, so
# every checked-in `docs/man/*.1` page compared unequal to its own freshly
# generated bytes on the Windows leg alone (CI run 33473165611). Anything
# else that compares a checked-in file byte-for-byte would have hit it next.
#
# Pinning the working tree to LF everywhere is the fix at the source rather
# than in the comparison. Nothing tracked here wants CRLF — no `.bat`,
# `.cmd`, or `.ps1` — and every tracked file is already LF in the index, so
# this needs no `--renormalize` pass.
* text=auto eol=lf
